  {
    "number": 73,
    "title": "Use shared caches and fnm for Node 24 in setup guidance",
    "body": "Refs #72\n\n## Summary\n\n`docs/development.md`:\n- Replaces the `npm ci --cache /tmp/pixoo-npm-cache` workaround and the sandbox `PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH` advice with guidance to use npm's default cache (`~/.npm`) and Playwright's default browser cache (`~/.cache/ms-playwright`). A read-only cache gets reported instead of redirected.\n- Adds that when `node --version` is not v24, commands run through `fnm exec --using=.nvmrc --` from the worktree root, reusing one shared Node 24 installation. This is the same guidance agent-device-hub documents.\n\n## Why\n\nOn 2026-09-23 the WSL host's RAM-backed `/tmp` filled completely, partly from caches and per-task Node installs. The Codex local-development sandbox profile now allows writes to `~/.npm` and `~/.cache/ms-playwright`. This repository requires Node 24 while the host default is Node 22, which had led agents to install Node per task.\n\n## Candidate evidence\n\n- Base: `71fbefcfdcf6163fc7180264436a6360cbc371ae` (origin/main). Head: `2134ab182f7f368c84f326039d79de7a96ed89b6`. Merge-base: the base.\n- Diff: `git diff 71fbefcfdcf6163fc7180264436a6360cbc371ae...2134ab182f7f368c84f326039d79de7a96ed89b6` (`docs/development.md` only). Worktree clean at head.\n- Validation at head, with Node v24.21.0 through `fnm exec --using=.nvmrc --` (the documented prefix): `npm ci` exit 0; `npm run check:workflow` exit 0 (18 of 18 items valid, inventory unchanged); `npm run test:workflow` exit 0 (10 of 10).\n\n## Scope notes\n\nDocumentation only; no application, simulator or device change, no OpenSpec change, no UI change. Related: #70 / #71 (cleanup after delivery).\n\n## Reviews\n\nIndependent Standards and Specification reviews pending.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
